    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#006",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:nutrition:00-overview, git-history:nutrition:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "nutrition/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "nutrition/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:nutrition:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nutrition",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "nutrition",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nutrition - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nNUTRIENTS\n├── MACRONUTRIENTS (gram-scale; primary energy and structural substrates)\n│   ├── Carbohydrates  4 kcal/g\n│   │   ├── Monosaccharides: glucose, fructose, galactose\n│   │   ├── Disaccharides: sucrose (Glc+Fru), lactose (Glc+Gal), maltose (Glc+Glc)\n│   │   ├── Polysaccharides: starch (α-1,4 linked; amylose + amylopectin)\n│   │   │                    glycogen (highly branched, α-1,6 + α-1,4)\n│   │   └── Dietary fiber: cellulose (β-1,4 — not human-digestible)\n│   │                      pectin, FOS, inulin — fermented by gut bacteria → SCFAs\n│   │\n│   ├── Proteins  4 kcal/g\n│   │   ├── 20 amino acids; 9 essential (cannot be synthesized):\n│   │   │   His, Ile, Leu, Lys, Met, Phe, Thr, Trp, Val\n│   │   ├── Conditionally essential (under stress): Arg, Gln, Gly, Cys, Tyr, Pro\n│   │   └── Functions: structural (collagen, actin, myosin), enzymatic,\n│   │                  signaling (insulin, GH), immune (antibodies), transport (Hb)\n│   │\n│   └── Fats (Lipids)  9 kcal/g\n│       ├── Saturated FA (SFA): no double bonds; C12:0 to C22:0\n│       │   Palmitic (C16:0), stearic (C18:0) — dominant in animal fat\n│       ├── Monounsaturated FA (MUFA): 1 double bond\n│       │   Oleic acid (C18:1 ω-9) — olive oil, avocado, majority of most fats\n│       ├── Polyunsaturated FA (PUFA): ≥2 double bonds\n│       │   omega-3: ALA (C18:3) from plants; EPA (C20:5) + DHA (C22:6) from fish\n│       │   omega-6: Linoleic acid (C18:2) from vegetable oils → AA (arachidonic)\n│       │   Essential: ALA + LA — humans lack Δ12 and Δ15 desaturase\n│       └── Trans FA: geometrically trans double bonds\n│           Industrial (partially hydrogenated): atherogenic — raises LDL, lowers HDL\n│           Ruminant (vaccenic acid, CLA): different metabolism, less harmful\n│\n├── MICRONUTRIENTS (milligram to microgram scale; catalytic and regulatory)\n│   ├── Vitamins (13 essential)\n│   │   ├── Fat-soluble (stored; toxicity possible): A, D, E, K\n│   │   └── Water-soluble (minimal storage; daily need): C + 8 B-vitamins\n│   │       B1 (thiamine), B2 (riboflavin), B3 (niacin), B5 (pantothenic),\n│   │       B6 (pyridoxine), B7 (biotin), B9 (folate), B12 (cobalamin)\n│   └── Minerals\n│       ├── Macrominerals (>100 mg/day): Ca, P, Mg, Na, K, Cl, S\n│       └── Trace minerals (<100 mg/day): Fe, Zn, Cu, Se, I, Mn, Cr, Mo, F\n│\n└── PHYTONUTRIENTS (non-essential; bioactive plant compounds)\n    ├── Polyphenols: flavonoids (quercetin, EGCG), stilbenes (resveratrol), lignans\n    ├── Carotenoids: β-carotene (pro-vitamin A), lycopene, lutein/zeaxanthin\n    └── Glucosinolates: cruciferous vegetables → indoles + isothiocyanates\n        (broccoli, Brussels sprouts, wasabi — bitter defensive compounds)\n```"
    },
